# Workspace repo scope

The parent `~/projects` directory (this workspace root) is an **orchestration workspace only** — not a single application repo.

## Git

- **Never** run `git init` in the parent workspace root.
- **Never** stage, commit, push, or otherwise use git against the parent workspace root as if it were one repo.
- Git operations (`status`, `diff`, `add`, `commit`, `push`, `pull`, branch/checkout) belong **only** inside an explicitly named repo directory (a top-level folder under `projects/` that has its own `.git`).

## Repo-scoped prompts

When a prompt **starts with** a bracketed repo list — e.g. `[synq-forge, synq-phalanx] …` — treat that list as the **active repo scope** for the entire turn unless the user explicitly widens it.

While scoped, restrict to those repo directories:

| Activity | Scope |
|----------|--------|
| File edits | Only paths under `<repo>/` for each named repo |
| Search / read | Prefer `<repo>/`; do not broad-search sibling repos or workspace root code |
| Terminal commands | `cd` into the target repo before running repo-specific commands |
| Migrations, builds, tests | Run inside the named repo only |
| Git | Only inside the named repo's directory |

Repo folder names match the bracket tokens (e.g. `[commonspace-app]` → `projects/commonspace-app/`).

## Orchestration paths (workspace root)

These workspace-meta paths are **not** application repos; writing here for orchestration is allowed even under a repo-scoped prompt:

- `.md/handoff/`, `.md/blueprints/`, `.md/reports/`
- `.cursor/rules/`, `.cursor/plans/`

Do **not** put application source, migrations, or deployable config in workspace root when a named repo exists for that project.

## Default when no scope prefix

- Do not modify files outside the repo clearly tied to the task.
- If the task spans multiple repos, confirm scope from the prompt, blueprint, or Linear task — do not assume the whole monorepo-style workspace is one git repo.
- Before any git command, verify the working directory is inside the intended repo (contains that repo's `.git`).

## Examples

```text
[synq-forge] fix live trader timer
→ edit/search/run commands only under synq-forge/; git only in synq-forge/

[commonspace-app, commonspace-ui-v3] deploy readiness
→ scope to those two folders; separate git blocks per repo

Add handoff for synq-forge work (no prefix)
→ may write .md/handoff/synq-forge/… at workspace root; code changes still under synq-forge/
```
